You are building the Openbank CX Signal Room dashboard.

Before making any decision, always read and use the reference folder:
frontend/public/swati-dashboard

This folder contains:
- Swati profile
- meeting transcript
- product feedback
- Openbank / Santander research
- public review research
- screenshots / existing dashboard references

Do not invent product direction from memory.
Do not copy the old Head of Credit Cards dashboard.
Use only its layout discipline if needed: compact dark cards, tight grids, clear rows, polished UI alignment.

The dashboard must be built from Swati feedback:
- lead with insight, not dashboard metrics
- daily-engagement surface
- top 3 best calls and top 3 worst calls
- internal calls/chats/emails/tickets first
- public reviews as one separate component only
- closed-loop customer pain recovery
- risk layer that shows UDAAP / Reg E / CFPB-like signals
- executive-ready but operationally useful

Never use the word "Swati" in the UI.
Never use wording that attacks the client's analytics team.
Never say "analytics team would not have surfaced this."
Never create play/pause/transcript/open-queue buttons.
Never put public grounding in every component.
Never include X/Twitter unless verified public grounding is available.
